    "['ppp authentication [method] [direction]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ppp authentication-mode pap', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nppp authentication-mode pap\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The Cisco command `ppp authentication pap callin` specifies PAP authentication for incoming PPP connections.\\n2. In HUAWEI devices, the equivalent command is `ppp authentication-mode pap`, which enables PAP authentication for both incoming and outgoing connections by default (HUAWEI doesn\\'t have the \"callin\" direction parameter like Cisco).\\n3. The HUAWEI command is simpler as it doesn\\'t distinguish between authentication directions (callin/callout) in the same way Cisco does.', 'trans_template': 'ppp authentication-mode pap'}]]": 1,
    "['ppp pap sent-username [username] password [encryption_type] [password]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ppp authentication-mode pap', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent HUAWEI command for the PPP PAP authentication configuration:\\n\\n##\\nppp authentication-mode pap\\nppp pap local-user rtb password cipher 13061E010803\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The first line enables PAP authentication on the interface (equivalent to `ppp authentication pap` in Cisco)\\n2. The second line configures the PAP username and password (equivalent to `ppp pap sent-username` in Cisco)\\n3. Note that Huawei uses \"local-user\" instead of \"sent-username\"\\n4. The \"cipher\" keyword in Huawei is equivalent to \"7\" in Cisco (indicating the password is encrypted)', 'trans_template': 'ppp authentication-mode pap'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'ppp pap local-user rtb password cipher 13061E010803', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent HUAWEI command for the PPP PAP authentication configuration:\\n\\n##\\nppp authentication-mode pap\\nppp pap local-user rtb password cipher 13061E010803\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The first line enables PAP authentication on the interface (equivalent to `ppp authentication pap` in Cisco)\\n2. The second line configures the PAP username and password (equivalent to `ppp pap sent-username` in Cisco)\\n3. Note that Huawei uses \"local-user\" instead of \"sent-username\"\\n4. The \"cipher\" keyword in Huawei is equivalent to \"7\" in Cisco (indicating the password is encrypted)', 'trans_template': 'ppp pap local-user rtb password cipher 13061E010803'}]]": 1,
